<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rutgers University</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1766</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Queen's College</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rutgers University is the state university of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, founded in 1766 as Queen's College by ministers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-reformed-church">Dutch Reformed Church</a>. Based in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, it was renamed in 1825 after the benefactor Henry Rutgers and became the state university in 1945. It is the eighth-oldest college in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rutgers-university.jpg" alt="Rutgers University" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rutgers_University_seal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
